## EnvironmentBoundary Component

This component enables conditional rendering based on the hosting environment. It follows a clean, minimal component design with focused responsibilities.

### Features
- Checks current environment via `IWebHostEnvironment`
- Supports `ChildContent` for simple conditional blocks
- Clear parameter naming following project conventions

### Usage
```razor
<EnvironmentBoundary Environment="Development">
    <p>Development-only content</p>
</EnvironmentBoundary>
```

### Implementation
```razor
@inject IWebHostEnvironment Environment

@if (IsMatchingEnvironment())
{
    @ChildContent
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Environment { get; set; } = "Production";
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; }

    private bool IsMatchingEnvironment()
    {
        return string.Equals(Environment, this.Environment.EnvironmentName, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
    }
}
```

